      "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Show failed account-link attempts inside the dialog**\n\nWhen the second Google request includes `linkAccount` and fails\u2014for example because the current password is wrong\u2014the catch path runs with `signupDialogOpen === false` and calls `setFormError(...)`, not `setGoogleError(...)`. This dialog only renders `googleError`, while the ordinary form error is obscured behind the open modal, so the user receives no visible failure feedback and cannot tell whether to correct the credentials or retry. Route link-attempt failures to the error state displayed here.\n\nUseful? React with \ud83d\udc4d\u00a0/ \ud83d\udc4e.",
